    "metadata": "{\"summary\":\"There is no scientific evidence supporting the claim that 5G technology causes COVID-19 or plays any role in the transmission of the virus. This myth originated from online misinformation and conspiracy theories that gained traction during the early months of the pandemic.bu+3​\\nScience and Disease Transmission\\nCOVID-19 is spread through respiratory droplets when infected people cough, sneeze, or talk; it is not transmitted via radio signals, electromagnetic waves, or mobile networks. 5G is simply a new generation of cellular network technology and does not emit radiation at levels that would cause viral transmission or mutation.joghr+2​\\nSpread of the Conspiracy Theory\\nThe rumor linking 5G and COVID-19 became widespread through social media posts and conspiracy-oriented websites, sometimes leading to damaging incidents such as arson attacks on cell towers in Europe. These ideas were amplified by distrust in government and misunderstanding of technology, but have been repeatedly debunked by health organizations and experts.pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih+3​\\nImpact of Belief in the Myth\\nIndividuals who believe 5G is linked to COVID-19 are less likely to comply with public health measures, which can hinder broader disease control efforts. Public health experts recommend education campaigns to combat this misinformation, focusing on the scientific reality and promoting trust in legitimate sources.latrobe+1​\\nIn summary, the idea that 5G causes COVID-19 is a conspiracy theory with no factual basis, and believing it can be harmful to individuals and communities.vox+3​\",\"citations\":[\"https://www.bu.edu/sph/news/articles/2021/5g-doesnt-cause-covid-19-but-myth-went-viral/\",\"https://www.joghr.org/article/17606-factors-associated-with-the-myth-about-5g-network-during-covid-19-pandemic-in-sub-saharan-africa\",\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7205032/\",\"https://www.latrobe.edu.au/news/articles/2020/opinion/5g-and-covid-19-conspiracy-theories\",\"https://www.vox.com/recode/2020/4/24/21231085/coronavirus-5g-conspiracy-theory-covid-facebook-youtube\"],\"extractionConfidence\":1,\"extractionWarnings\":[]}"
